---
import '@fontsource-variable/archivo/wdth.css';
import '@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono';
import '../styles/base.css';
import '../styles/page.css';
import '../styles/stage.css';
import archivo from '@fontsource-variable/archivo/files/archivo-latin-wdth-normal.woff2?url';
import jetbrains from '@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono/files/jetbrains-mono-latin-wght-normal.woff2?url';
import Chapter from '../components/Chapter.astro';
import Close from '../components/Close.astro';
import Download from '../components/Download.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Keys from '../components/Keys.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Remote from '../components/Remote.astro';
import Sheets from '../components/Sheets.astro';
import Badge from '../components/stage/Badge.astro';
import Stage from '../components/stage/Stage.astro';
import stillAgent from '../assets/stills/agent.webp';
import stillBrowser from '../assets/stills/browser.webp';
import stillChanges from '../assets/stills/changes.webp';
import stillFlow from '../assets/stills/flow.webp';

const title = 'cornercase gpui · All your agents, one native window';
const description =
  'A native window for cornercase, the terminal multiplexer for running coding agents in parallel. Drawn on the GPU with GPUI, on macOS, Linux and Windows.';
const origin = (Astro.site?.toString() ?? '').replace(/\/$/, '');
const base = (import.meta.env.SITE_BASE ?? '').replace(/\/$/, '');
const site = `${origin}${base}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${site}/`} />
    <link rel="icon" href="./favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin href={archivo} />
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin href={jetbrains} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0c0e" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={`${site}/`} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={`${site}/og.png`} />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={`${site}/og.png`} />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var root = document.documentElement;
        root.classList.add('js');
        if (!window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches && window.WebGL2RenderingContext && window.innerHeight >= 300) {
          root.classList.add('motion', 'intro');
          setTimeout(function () {
            if (!window.cornercaseAlive) root.classList.remove('motion', 'intro');
          }, 4000);
        }
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <canvas class="field" data-field aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <Nav />
    <Hero />
    <Stage />
    <main id="main">
      <Chapter id="layers" title="Drawn on|the GPU." side="left">
        <p>GPUI, the framework behind the Zed editor, draws every card, glyph and shadow. The window is glass in layers, and where your system can blur it, your desktop shows through.</p>
        <ol class="layers" data-layers>
          <li data-layer-name="ground"><b>Ground</b><span>one sheet of glass</span></li>
          <li data-layer-name="rail"><b>Rail</b><span>every panel, a click away</span></li>
          <li data-layer-name="side"><b>Sidebar</b><span>projects, workspaces, agents</span></li>
          <li data-layer-name="panes"><b>Panes</b><span>a floating card each</span></li>
          <li data-layer-name="dock"><b>Dock</b><span>the work beside the terminal</span></li>
        </ol>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="status" title="Know who|needs you." side="right" still={stillAgent} alt="The sidebar, with each agent's status, model and context.">
        <p>Every agent's status, model and context in the sidebar, beside each workspace's pull request and how its checks went. View context says what fills it, and spends no tokens. When one needs you, a toast, a notification and a sound say so.</p>
        <ul class="statuses" data-statuses>
          <li data-status="working"><Badge status="working" size={22} /><b>Working</b></li>
          <li data-status="waiting"><Badge status="waiting" size={22} /><b>Waiting</b></li>
          <li data-status="failed"><Badge status="failed" size={22} /><b>Failed</b></li>
          <li data-status="done"><Badge status="done" size={22} /><b>Done</b></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cap__keys"><Keys keys={['cmd', 'B']} /> the agent that needs you</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="panes" title="Every pane,|a floating|card." side="left">
        <p>Split with a key, drag the gap between cards to resize, and drag a pane by its handle onto another to move it. Drop a file to paste it. Paste a screenshot, and the agent can open it.</p>
        <p class="cap__keys"><Keys keys={['cmd', 'D']} /> split right <Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'D']} /> split down</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="preview" title="Rest on a|path. See|the file." side="right">
        <p>Rest the pointer on a path a program printed and the file shows beside it: code at its lines, images, PDFs and documents. Rest it on a web address and the page shows.</p>
        <ul class="beats" data-preview-beats>
          <li>Code, at its lines</li>
          <li>The page of a local address</li>
          <li>Images and documents</li>
        </ul>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="review" title="Review|beside|the agent." side="left" still={stillChanges} alt="The Changes panel docked right of the terminal.">
        <p>The workspace's diff, to filter by path, stage, discard and review, and a merge check that names the files that would conflict before you merge. Files has the tree with git's letters, a viewer that marks what changed and can take the whole width, and search. Select lines or characters in either to ask the agent about them, find in the open file, and wrap long lines or cut them. TODO holds what you still have to do, one click from an agent. Recap has an agent sum up what your agents did, each conversation a link to its pane.</p>
        <p class="cap__keys"><Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'C']} /> Changes <Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'E']} /> Files <Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'L']} /> TODO <Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'H']} /> Recap</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="browser" title="A browser|beside|the agent." side="left" still={stillBrowser} alt="The Browser panel showing a checkout page from a local dev server, beside a terminal.">
        <p>A real Chrome on the workspace's dev servers, with device sizes and the console. Pick an element or take a screenshot and hand it to the agent. When the agent finishes, the page reloads.</p>
        <p class="cap__keys"><Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'B']} /> Browser</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter id="flow" title="A team,|lit up." side="left" still={stillFlow} alt="The Flow panel: a run called Full issue, with its task and its team of five agents.">
        <p>A flow is a team of agents run by an orchestrator. Its plan lights up where the work stands, beside the agents at work, with the messages they send each other. Write your own in its sheet: long prompts, stages you move up and down, the plan redrawn as you go.</p>
        <p class="cap__keys"><Keys keys={['shift', 'cmd', 'F']} /> Flow</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Sheets />
      <Close />
      <Remote />
      <Download />
    </main>
    <Footer />
    <script>
      import '../client/main';
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
